meta {
  name: Get Space Credential (space.getSpaceCredential)
  type: http
  seq: 141
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.getSpaceCredential
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  DPoP: {{dpopProof}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{delegationToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "space": "at://did:plc:exampleauthority/space/org.example.bucket/self"
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:8080
  delegationToken: <token from getDelegationToken on the user's PDS>
  dpopProof: <ES256 dpop+jwt: htm POST, htu {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.getSpaceCredential, fresh iat, jti; no ath, no nonce>
}

docs {
  Atproto Spaces (proposal 0016). Called on the space authority's PDS: exchanges the delegation
  token (the request's Authorization token) plus a mint-time DPoP proof for a 2 h space
  credential (`typ atproto-space-credential+jwt`, `kid #atproto_space`, no `aud`, `cnf.jkt` =
  the proof key's RFC 7638 thumbprint). The credential is then presented to repo hosts as
  `Authorization: DPoP <credential>` with a per-request proof carrying `ath`.

  Errors (lexicon names): SpaceNotFound (unknown, or not anchored on an account here),
  SpaceDeleted, InvalidDelegationToken (bad signature/typ/kid/sub/aud/exp, or already used —
  the token is single-use), UserNotAuthorized (member-list policy; the managing-app policy is not
  evaluated yet), AppNotAuthorized (allow-list app access needs client attestation, not yet
  verified). Optional body field `clientAttestation` is accepted and currently ignored.
}
